    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `ageBand` derivation from an optional `birthDate`, computed against `registrationDate`. The endpoint pipelines (`RequireOwnerFields \u2192 BuildOwner \u2192 \u2026 \u2192 RespondWithOwner*`) were left untouched \u2014 everything hangs off the existing mapper and DTO-generation seams, so no function grew and no large class was edited.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added optional `birthDate` (date) to the `OwnerFields` request schema and read-only `ageBand` to the `Owner` response schema. Both DTO fields regenerate automatically; MapStruct auto-maps `birthDate` both ways by name.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `birthDate` field (`birth_date` column) with a getter/setter, mirroring `registrationDate`. Persistence is required because the test reads the band back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n3. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql` + `data.sql`** \u2014 added the `birth_date DATE` column (the test DB runs `ddl-auto=none`) and a `NULL` value to the seed owner rows.\n\n4. **`AgeBand.java`** (new) \u2014 a small pure helper, sibling to `MembershipNumber`/`CheckDigit`: returns `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), `SENIOR` (65+) via `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate)`, or `null` when either date is absent.\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one `@Mapping` line wiring `ageBand` through `AgeBand.of(...)`, exactly the pattern the other derived fields already use. Because all three responders (create/GET/update) funnel through `toOwnerDto`, this single line covers every path.\n\nThe test's owner (`birthDate=1990-01-01`, registered today, 2026-09-04) resolves to age 36 \u2192 `ADULT`, as asserted.",
